1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,632
Good morning, I'm Whale Girl. Today is October 7.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:04,452
Seven stories today:

3
00:00:04,472 --> 00:00:07,012
Mistral's trillion-parameter model,

4
00:00:07,032 --> 00:00:14,232
Reflection's open-weight model Beam,

5
00:00:14,252 --> 00:00:14,552
OpenAI watermarks ChatGPT text,

6
00:00:14,572 --> 00:00:14,872
Anthropic gives startups a free year

7
00:00:14,757 --> 00:00:15,057
of Claude Team,

8
00:00:14,872 --> 00:00:17,272
Anthropic expands its cyber verification program,

9
00:00:17,292 --> 00:02:21,610
Together Link

10
00:02:21,630 --> 00:02:36,600
runs open models in Claude Code,

11
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:51,062
and Google's multimodal embedding model.

12
00:02:51,082 --> 00:02:51,866
First, a one-trillion-parameter model

13
00:02:51,886 --> 00:02:52,603
that activates only 49B for each token.

14
00:02:52,623 --> 00:02:54,653
On October 6, French company Mistral

15
00:02:54,673 --> 00:02:56,113
released Mistral Large 4

16
00:02:56,133 --> 00:02:57,735
as a public preview,

17
00:02:57,755 --> 00:02:59,144
with API access.

18
00:02:59,164 --> 00:03:01,005
It was trained in Mistral's own European

19
00:03:01,025 --> 00:03:02,370
data centers on 3,800 NVIDIA

20
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:04,293
Grace Blackwell GPUs.

21
00:03:04,313 --> 00:03:06,081
The weights won't come until the end of October,

22
00:03:06,101 --> 00:03:07,866
and the license will be announced then.

23
00:03:07,886 --> 00:03:10,016
Its headline claim is security work:

24
00:03:10,036 --> 00:03:12,920
82% on a test of reproducing open-source vulnerabilities.

25
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:15,094
The Decoder says Opus 5.5

26
00:03:15,114 --> 00:03:17,515
and GPT-6 Astra score near zero

27
00:03:17,535 --> 00:03:19,645
on it because they refuse the task.

28
00:03:19,665 --> 00:03:22,571
On the overall Intelligence Index, though, it scores 38

29
00:03:22,591 --> 00:03:24,664
against Opus 5.5's 58.

30
00:03:24,684 --> 00:03:27,021
Finding bugs doesn't make it strong at everything.

31
00:03:27,041 --> 00:03:29,041
Wait for the weights.

32
00:03:29,241 --> 00:03:32,162
Second, US startup Reflection AI

33
00:03:32,182 --> 00:03:35,063
released Beam, its first open-weight model.

34
00:03:35,083 --> 00:03:36,846
It's a mixture of experts

35
00:03:36,866 --> 00:03:39,834
with 501B total parameters and 23B active.

36
00:03:39,854 --> 00:03:40,924
It handles text only,

37
00:03:40,944 --> 00:03:42,899
with a one-million-token context window

38
00:03:42,919 --> 00:03:45,971
and 23.8T tokens of pre-training.

39
00:03:45,991 --> 00:03:48,873
Weights and technical details will come in October

40
00:03:48,893 --> 00:03:50,791
through major cloud providers.

41
00:03:50,811 --> 00:03:53,671
Reflection says it matches Zhipu's GLM-5.2

42
00:03:53,691 --> 00:03:56,489
while using 3 to 4 times less inference compute.

43
00:03:56,509 --> 00:03:58,891
It's backed by NVIDIA and Sequoia Capital,

44
00:03:58,911 --> 00:04:00,625
with about $4.7 billion raised.

45
00:04:00,645 --> 00:04:03,088
These performance numbers are all the company's own,

46
00:04:03,108 --> 00:04:04,352
not independently verified.

47
00:04:04,372 --> 00:04:07,526
The weights aren't out yet, so hold off on conclusions.

48
00:04:07,726 --> 00:04:09,938
Third, OpenAI is adding to ChatGPT's

49
00:04:09,958 --> 00:04:12,187
text an invisible watermark.

50
00:04:12,207 --> 00:04:14,062
On October 5, OpenAI announced

51
00:04:14,082 --> 00:04:16,277
that in the coming weeks it will first give EU users'

52
00:04:16,297 --> 00:04:17,635
text a watermark.

53
00:04:17,655 --> 00:04:19,823
It covers ChatGPT and Codex,

54
00:04:19,843 --> 00:04:22,305
and the reason is compliance with the EU AI Act.

55
00:04:22,325 --> 00:04:24,017
The watermark is called textGrain.

56
00:04:24,037 --> 00:04:25,571
It subtly shapes word choices,

57
00:04:25,591 --> 00:04:29,155
leaving a pattern people can't see but a detector can.

58
00:04:29,175 --> 00:04:30,356
API developers

59
00:04:30,376 --> 00:04:33,042
can opt in right now, anywhere.

60
00:04:33,062 --> 00:04:35,322
But a few edits weaken it.

61
00:04:35,342 --> 00:04:37,538
Swapping 10% of words for synonyms

62
00:04:37,558 --> 00:04:40,272
cuts detection from about 92% to 66%.

63
00:04:40,292 --> 00:04:41,699
Short passages, math answers

64
00:04:41,719 --> 00:04:44,269
and translated text are harder to detect.

65
00:04:44,289 --> 00:04:45,448
OpenAI also says

66
00:04:45,468 --> 00:04:48,067
that a missing watermark doesn't prove a human wrote it.

67
00:04:48,267 --> 00:04:50,070
Fourth, Anthropic

68
00:04:50,090 --> 00:04:53,531
is giving startups a free year of Claude Team.

69
00:04:53,551 --> 00:04:54,887
On October 6, Anthropic

70
00:04:54,907 --> 00:04:56,992
expanded its Claude for Startups program:

71
00:04:57,012 --> 00:04:59,099
a free year of Claude Team,

72
00:04:59,119 --> 00:05:00,516
with up to 5 seats.

73
00:05:00,536 --> 00:05:02,772
It also adds $1,000 in API credits.

74
00:05:02,792 --> 00:05:04,478
Startups also get access to Claude Marketplace

75
00:05:04,498 --> 00:05:05,123
for building plugins,

76
00:05:05,143 --> 00:05:07,941
and virtual office hours with Anthropic's Applied AI team.

77
00:05:07,961 --> 00:05:10,456
There are two conditions, and meeting either is enough:

78
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:12,138
founded within the last 5 years,

79
00:05:12,158 --> 00:05:14,442
or funded within the last 2.

80
00:05:14,462 --> 00:05:15,933
The article lists no regional limit.

81
00:05:15,953 --> 00:05:16,504
Applications go

82
00:05:16,524 --> 00:05:19,213
through the Claude for Startups program page.

83
00:05:19,233 --> 00:05:20,820
Anthropic's argument is that most people

84
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:23,494
will get AI's benefits through the companies

85
00:05:23,514 --> 00:05:25,709
that build on top of models.

86
00:05:25,729 --> 00:05:26,913
The free ride lasts one year,

87
00:05:26,933 --> 00:05:29,203
so decide what to build with it.

88
00:05:29,403 --> 00:05:30,750
Fifth, Anthropic merged

89
00:05:30,770 --> 00:05:33,033
two cyber programs into one,

90
00:05:33,053 --> 00:05:35,103
open to more defenders.

91
00:05:35,123 --> 00:05:36,430
October 6: the expanded

92
00:05:36,450 --> 00:05:38,339
Cyber Verification Program

93
00:05:38,359 --> 00:05:38,759
is live,

94
00:05:38,779 --> 00:05:40,802
combining Project Glasswing

95
00:05:40,822 --> 00:05:42,557
and the original verification program.

96
00:05:42,577 --> 00:05:44,024
Verified security professionals

97
00:05:44,044 --> 00:05:45,637
get stronger cyber capabilities

98
00:05:45,657 --> 00:05:48,754
and fewer blocking classifiers.

99
00:05:48,774 --> 00:05:50,294
There are three tiers:

100
00:05:50,314 --> 00:05:52,965
Defense, Red Team and Specialized access.

101
00:05:52,985 --> 00:05:54,636
Defense is for work like incident response

102
00:05:54,656 --> 00:05:55,935
and malware analysis.

103
00:05:55,955 --> 00:05:58,239
Individuals and open-source maintainers

104
00:05:58,259 --> 00:06:00,793
can apply, with a reply in a few days.

105
00:06:00,813 --> 00:06:03,085
Red Team adds authorized penetration testing.

106
00:06:03,105 --> 00:06:05,209
It's for organizations only, with a wait of a few weeks.

107
00:06:05,229 --> 00:06:07,349
Specialized access is for flight systems,

108
00:06:07,369 --> 00:06:10,172
power grids and other safety-critical testing,

109
00:06:10,192 --> 00:06:11,291
with limited slots.

110
00:06:11,311 --> 00:06:13,368
It covers Claude Opus 5.5,

111
00:06:13,388 --> 00:06:15,817
Sonnet 5.5 and Mythos 5.1,

112
00:06:15,837 --> 00:06:18,451
plus new models going forward.

113
00:06:18,471 --> 00:06:21,730
If you do vulnerability research, check which tier you fit.

114
00:06:21,930 --> 00:06:24,084
Sixth, you use Claude Code

115
00:06:24,104 --> 00:06:25,536
but run open models behind it,

116
00:06:25,556 --> 00:06:27,603
and there's now a ready-made tool.

117
00:06:27,623 --> 00:06:29,508
Together AI released Together Link, a free,

118
00:06:29,528 --> 00:06:32,353
MIT-licensed command-line tool

119
00:06:32,373 --> 00:06:34,018
that's now in beta.

120
00:06:34,038 --> 00:06:35,501
It connects Claude Code,

121
00:06:35,521 --> 00:06:36,963
Codex, OpenCode,

122
00:06:36,983 --> 00:06:40,260
and the Claude and ChatGPT desktop apps.

123
00:06:40,280 --> 00:06:41,121
In Claude Code,

124
00:06:41,141 --> 00:06:43,414
the Opus tier runs Kimi K3

125
00:06:43,434 --> 00:06:45,818
and the Fable tier runs GLM 5.3.

126
00:06:45,838 --> 00:06:47,057
By default, an auto router

127
00:06:47,077 --> 00:06:49,183
sends simple requests to Together's models

128
00:06:49,203 --> 00:06:51,183
and hard ones to Claude Opus.

129
00:06:51,203 --> 00:06:52,437
Routing to Opus requires

130
00:06:52,457 --> 00:06:55,100
that you connect your own Anthropic API key.

131
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:57,730
Note the tool is free, but the models aren't:

132
00:06:57,750 --> 00:06:59,331
Together's models are billed

133
00:06:59,351 --> 00:07:01,170
at its standard rates.

134
00:07:01,190 --> 00:07:03,400
It supports only macOS and Linux

135
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:06,080
for now, and needs a Together API key.

136
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:07,663
Does swapping models save money?

137
00:07:07,683 --> 00:07:09,025
Work it out.

138
00:07:09,225 --> 00:07:10,934
Seventh, Google DeepMind

139
00:07:10,954 --> 00:07:12,840
released a 740M-parameter

140
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:15,217
open multimodal embedding model.

141
00:07:15,237 --> 00:07:16,404
An embedding model turns

142
00:07:16,424 --> 00:07:18,037
content into a list of numbers,

143
00:07:18,057 --> 00:07:20,281
so it can be searched and compared.

144
00:07:20,301 --> 00:07:22,937
EmbeddingGemma 2 puts text, images,

145
00:07:22,957 --> 00:07:25,799
video and audio into one vector space.

146
00:07:25,819 --> 00:07:29,411
The output is 768 dimensions, and you can truncate it to 512,

147
00:07:29,431 --> 00:07:31,941
256 or 128 to save space.

148
00:07:31,961 --> 00:07:33,574
It's built on Gemma 4,

149
00:07:33,594 --> 00:07:35,521
with an 8,192-token context window and support

150
00:07:35,541 --> 00:07:37,359
for more than 100 languages.

151
00:07:37,379 --> 00:07:39,049
It's under the Apache 2.0 license,

152
00:07:39,069 --> 00:07:40,832
with weights released the same day.

153
00:07:40,852 --> 00:07:43,132
It's designed for everyday devices like phones and laptops,

154
00:07:43,152 --> 00:07:46,260
which makes local multimodal search much easier.

155
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:49,300
If you build search or Q&A, it's ready to try.

156
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:52,150
That's all for today. Sources are in the description.

157
00:07:52,170 --> 00:07:53,523
See you tomorrow.
